## Your tips

**My sales** shows **My tips**: your share of each tip, half when you sold the rental, half when you did the handover, all of it when you did both. Paid with your pay.

## Extensions and weekly payments (release 50)

You earn commission on an extension or a weekly payment only when you started it. One the renter asked for in their account, a weekly payment the site made by itself, or one Admin handled earns no commission. Ask an Admin to give it to you with **Give to** when you did the work.
',
  '<p class="gd-p">Sales (and field staff) earn a commission on the rentals they source: a renter you found yourself. Say so when you enter the rental, the quote or the offer. Customer service, Fleet and Finance earn no commission and no sales credit: your help is credited on the booking (Helped by) and on your scorecard.</p><section class="gd-task" id="commissions-mark-who-found-the-client" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Mark who found the client</h2><p class="gd-p">Every rental, quote and offer you enter asks: <b class="gd-ui">I sourced this client</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Entered for CarmaCars</b>.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Choose <b class="gd-ui">I sourced this client</b> when you found the renter yourself: someone you know, your own post or your own outreach.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Choose <b class="gd-ui">Entered for CarmaCars</b> when the renter came to CarmaCars: the website, the phone line, a walk-in, a partner.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">A website request earns nothing by itself. If you sourced it anyway, choose I sourced this client on its offer: an Admin decides.</div></li></ol></div><div class="gd-tablewrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Table"><table class="gd-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col"></th><th scope="col">Commission</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Sales</td><td>Commission only, with no base pay. By the rental days of the month, on all of that month&#39;s rentals: in person under 50 days 10%, from 50 days 15%, from 100 days 20%; remote 5%, 10% and 15%, one tier lower in a month under 400 touches (chapter Sales)</td></tr><tr><td>Customer service, Fleet, Finance</td><td>No commission and no sales credit, whichever you choose above. Your help is credited as Helped by on the booking and counted on your scorecard</td></tr><tr><td>An owner you bring in (Sales)</td><td>What you ask for and an Admin approves: a flat amount at the owner&#39;s first paid rental, or a percent of their cars&#39; rentals for a time (chapter Sales). A CarmaCars expense: it never changes the owner&#39;s revenue</td></tr><tr><td>How much</td><td>The rate on the rental charge before tax, after discounts, with late extra days, plus the add-ons (release 35: the same rate on each confirmed add-on&#39;s own charge before tax; not prepaid fuel). Never on delivery, kilometres, young driver, the Protection Plan or other fees. Only a refund of the rental charge, or an add-on removed after booking, comes off</td></tr><tr><td>When earned</td><td>When the rental is completed and paid in full. Never on a cancelled, refunded, unpaid or charged-back rental, or on your own or a household rental</td></tr><tr><td>Your home address</td><td>It must be in your profile. Until it is, a commission waits as not earned yet, and you cannot add a rental or mark I sourced this client</td></tr><tr><td>Paid</td><td>After an Admin approves it, by transfer or on your pay statement. My sales shows each step: not earned yet, pending approval, approved, paid, reversed</td></tr></tbody></table></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>A refund or chargeback after a commission was paid comes off your next payment. Your staff agreement has the full rule.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="commissions-your-tips" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Your tips</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">My sales</b> shows <b class="gd-ui">My tips</b>: your share of each tip, half when you sold the rental, half when you did the handover, all of it when you did both. Paid with your pay.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="commissions-extensions-and-weekly-payments-release-50" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Extensions and weekly payments (release 50)</h2><p class="gd-p">You earn commission on an extension or a weekly payment only when you started it. One the renter asked for in their account, a weekly payment the site made by itself, or one Admin handled earns no commission. Ask an Admin to give it to you with <b class="gd-ui">Give to</b> when you did the work.</p></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('field', 'my-hours-and-pay', 'chapter', 'photo-shoots', 'Jobs are put on shifts: claim a shift and its jobs are yours. Your hours are paid every two weeks at your hourly rate (CA$18.00 an hour unless your agreement says another rate), with the commissions an Admin has approved.

## My shifts

Shifts are published by themselves, up to 14 days ahead: one shift of 10:00 to 17:00 every second day, and a shift of its own for a handover or return no shift covers. Fleet may add or cancel shifts too.

1. **Free to claim**: shifts someone gave up (first to claim takes it) and open shifts. Each shows the jobs already on it, for example "On it: 3 pickups, 1 return, 2 cleans". Press **Claim this shift**: its jobs are yours on **Today** and here. You can claim once you passed the academy.
2. **Coming up**: your shifts, each with the shift''s jobs and the work planned for you. It updates as bookings come in. Sharing a shift? Its jobs are split between you, least busy first; the others'' show on **Today** under **Also on your shift**, and **Take it** takes one.
3. Cannot work one? Press **Give this shift up** and say why. It is offered at once to everyone free then, and its jobs go with it to whoever claims it. Under 24 hours before the start it is marked late on your record.
4. **Swap with someone**: choose their shift and press **Ask for the swap**. They press **Accept the swap** or **Decline**. Each of you takes the other shift''s jobs.
5. **Past shifts**: each day with your hours, the jobs, the photos and the money you spent.
6. **Money you spent**: each one with where it stands. No receipt yet? Take the photo and press **Add the receipt**.


### Your shifts in Google Calendar

On **My shifts** (and on **Profile**), **Add my shifts and townhalls to Google Calendar** gives you a private link with the shifts you claimed, the tasks given to you and the weekly townhall. Press **Make my calendar link**, then **Add to Google Calendar** and **Add** in Google. New and changed shifts show by themselves; Google refreshes every few hours. Keep the link to yourself: **Regenerate link** stops the old one.

## Clock in and out

Clock in and out on **Today**, with your shift. Forgot to clock out, or a time is wrong? Tell Fleet: they fix it, say why, and the change is written in a log.

## Pay details

Before your first pay, **My pay** asks for your pay details: your full legal name, email, phone, SIN and a photo of a void cheque. Press **Save my pay details**. Your SIN is kept encrypted: only Finance and Admin can see it, every look is recorded, and you see only its last 3 digits. How you are paid (bank, e-Transfer) is just below.

## Your pay and your pay statements

A pay period is two weeks, Sunday to Saturday. An Admin runs the pay after it ends.

1. The pay is your hours times your hourly rate, plus the commissions and referral fees an Admin approved by the end of the period (see Commissions). Overtime and vacation pay are added only if CarmaCars has switched them on.
2. An Admin approves the pay run, pays you (by e-Transfer, bank transfer or cash) and records it. You get an email with the amount and how you were paid.
3. Under Pay statements on **My pay**, press **PDF** for the statement of a period: your hours day by day, the amounts, the commissions in it and how it was paid.

> Tip: A pay statement shows no income tax, CPP or EI. They are not worked out in the portal: for your tax slips, ask CarmaCars or your accountant.

## Where you clock in and out

The phone asks for your location once when you clock in and once when you clock out, and never in between. Allow it. If it is off, or you are more than 500 m from the lot, you can still clock in or out: write why in the box that appears, and Fleet sees it.

## Availability, standing shifts and the minimum (release 35)

1. Set when you can work (mornings, afternoons and evenings for each weekday, plus a note) on Welcome; change it later on My shifts or Profile.
2. My shifts opens as a week calendar: tap a shift to claim it. The cards are on the List tab.
3. A standing weekly shift, such as every Saturday 10 to 6, claims each matching published shift by itself up to two weeks ahead. Drop one date (the give-up rules apply) or end it.
4. Hold at least the minimum (2 shifts in 7 days by default). Under it, you get a daily reminder and a To do.
5. Pay stubs come every two weeks under My pay, with a PDF and an email once paid.

## Your tips

**My pay** shows **My tips**: your half of each tip on a car you handed over (all of it when you also sold the rental). A tip given to you in cash: tell the office, they record it on the booking''s Money tab.
', 'My shifts and My pay', 'Claim, give up and swap shifts, what you did on each, your hours, pay statements and pay details.',
